        "# Regularization Techniques in Deep Learning\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook demonstrates three techniques that can help improve neural-network training and generalization:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Dropout** – randomly disables a fraction of neurons during training.\n",
        "2. **Gradient clipping** – limits gradients to reduce unstable updates.\n",
        "3. **Early stopping** – stops training when validation performance stops improving.\n",
        "\n",
        "We use a synthetic binary-classification dataset for Dropout and Gradient Clipping, and MNIST for Early Stopping with two output tasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Note:** Gradient clipping is primarily an optimization/stability technique rather than a regularization method in the strict sense. It is included here because it helps control training behavior.\n"
      ]
    },
